{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794769085,"nonce":"zsiXvx81CQxLyDo+ngBNl3/874I=","title":"A CSS transition that has settled asks for the display's frame rate for as long as its node is on screen","message":"`CssAnimationStore::has_visible_vsync_class` (render_state.rs) looked at every animation and transition entry on a painted node, not only those that are playing. A settled entry stays in the store so the same target does not restart it, and its last values still named a layout property (the cn progress bar's `flex-grow`, an accordion's height), so `needs_vsync_for_smoothness` stayed true. In the owner's window, with the indeterminate bar on screen and nothing else going on, the trace had `css_vsync_class` true on 2,342 of 2,386 frames; with the filter on `is_playing` it is false on all of them.\n\nThe consequence is that a configured frame-rate cap, and the ambient cap that goes with it, were bypassed on every frame once such a transition had run. Test: overlay_css_active in blinc_recorder (a settled layout transition does not ask for vsync; it fails without the fix on that assertion).\n\nLabels: bug, perf, area:layout.","files":null}]}